  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two blocks (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>) are arranged on a horizontal frictionless table as shown in the figure. The coefficient of static friction between the two blocks is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math> Then the maximum horizontal force that can be applied on the larger block so that the blocks move together is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>.</mo></math> (Round off to the Nearest Integer) [Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi></math>&nbsp;as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0101_15a1fd32fa49.png\" style=\"width: 222px; height: 110px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "21",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p>"
  }
